    {
      "t": "list",
      "items": [
        [
          {
            "t": "Zoning (Vancouver): The City of Vancouver Zoning and Development Bylaw 3575 governs. In the R1-1 district the minimum site area is 306 m² for a house, a duplex, or a 3–4-unit multiple dwelling (10.0 m frontage), 464 m² for 5 units, and 557 m² for 6–8 units; a house may include a secondary suite plus a laneway house, and the multiplex form runs up to 6 strata units / 8 rental units."
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "t": "SSMUH position (Vancouver): R1-1 is the SSMUH framework where it applies — the duplex is the baseline two-unit form inside it, and the multiplex ladder above is the same framework's larger forms. SSMUH adds unit potential on a lot; it does not by itself split a duplex into separately titled halves."
          }
        ]
      ],
      "gen": "dx",
