      "gen": "dx",
      "q": "What extra calendar does a Vancouver duplex owner carry?",
      "a": "Advance taxes in February, main taxes in July, and the annual Empty Homes Tax property status declaration by the 2nd business day in February under By-law No. 11674 — the 3% Empty Homes Tax is Vancouver-only."
    },
    {
      "q": "When are property taxes due on a Vancouver home?",
      "a": "To the City of Vancouver, twice a year: advance taxes were due February 3, 2026 and main taxes were due July 3, 2026, with a 5% penalty on unpaid balances after the main-tax deadline.",
      "gen": "muse"
    },
    {
      "q": "What is the Empty Homes Tax declaration?",
      "a": "Every Vancouver residential property owner must submit an annual property status declaration on or before the 2nd business day in February under Vacancy Tax By-law No. 11674; a vacancy tax that remains unpaid as of the 10th business day of April bears a 5% penalty.",
      "gen": "muse"
    },
    {
